const SHL=[{"sa": "कर्मण्येवाधिकारस्ते मा फलेषु कदाचन ।<br>मा कर्मफलहेतुर्भूर्मा ते सङ्गोऽस्त्वकर्मणि ॥", "tr": "karmaṇy-evādhikāras te mā phaleṣu kadācana | mā karma-phala-hetur bhūr mā te saṅgo ’stv akarmaṇi ||", "en": "You have the right to your actions alone, never to their fruits. Let the fruit of action not be your motive, nor let attachment to inaction be yours.", "tk": "Master the process, not the outcome. Follow your plan, risk and entry rules on every trade; profit is the by-product, not the target.", "src": "Bhagavad Gītā 2.47"}, {"sa": "योगस्थः कुरु कर्माणि सङ्गं त्यक्त्वा धनञ्जय ।<br>सिद्ध्यसिद्ध्योः समो भूत्वा समत्वं योग उच्यते ॥", "tr": "yoga-sthaḥ kuru karmāṇi saṅgaṃ tyaktvā dhanañjaya | siddhy-asiddhyoḥ samo bhūtvā samatvaṃ yoga ucyate ||", "en": "Established in yoga, perform your actions, O Dhananjaya, giving up attachment and remaining even-minded in success and failure. Such evenness of mind is called yoga.", "tk": "Stay level after a big win and after a stop-loss. Emotional balance protects your capital more than any indicator.", "src": "Bhagavad Gītā 2.48"}, {"sa": "क्रोधाद्भवति सम्मोहः सम्मोहात्स्मृतिविभ्रमः ।<br>स्मृतिभ्रंशाद् बुद्धिनाशो बुद्धिनाशात्प्रणश्यति ॥", "tr": "krodhād bhavati sammohaḥ sammohāt smṛti-vibhramaḥ | smṛti-bhraṃśād buddhi-nāśo buddhi-nāśāt praṇaśyati ||", "en": "From anger arises delusion; from delusion, loss of memory; from loss of memory, the ruin of intelligence; and with the ruin of intelligence, one is lost.", "tk": "Revenge trading starts with anger after a loss. Close the platform, take a breath and return only when your mind is clear.", "src": "Bhagavad Gītā 2.63"}, {"sa": "सहसा विदधीत न क्रियाम् अविवेकः परमापदां पदम् ।<br>वृणते हि विमृश्यकारिणं गुणलुब्धाः स्वयमेव सम्पदः ॥", "tr": "sahasā vidadhīta na kriyām avivekaḥ paramāpadāṃ padam | vṛṇate hi vimṛśya-kāriṇaṃ guṇa-lubdhāḥ svayam eva sampadaḥ ||", "en": "Do not act in haste; lack of discernment is the home of the greatest calamities. Prosperity herself, drawn to merit, chooses the one who acts after careful thought.", "tk": "No impulsive entries. Wait for the A+ setup, confirm it, then act.", "src": "Kirātārjunīya 2.30 · Bhāravi"}, {"sa": "उद्यमेन हि सिध्यन्ति कार्याणि न मनोरथैः ।<br>न हि सुप्तस्य सिंहस्य प्रविशन्ति मुखे मृगाः ॥", "tr": "udyamena hi sidhyanti kāryāṇi na manorathaiḥ | na hi suptasya siṃhasya praviśanti mukhe mṛgāḥ ||", "en": "Tasks are accomplished through effort, not through mere wishes; deer do not walk into the mouth of a sleeping lion.", "tk": "Hope is not a strategy. Study the charts, journal your trades and put in the screen time.", "src": "Hitopadeśa · Subhāṣita"}, {"sa": "क्षणशः कणशश्चैव विद्यामर्थं च साधयेत् ।<br>क्षणत्यागे कुतो विद्या कणत्यागे कुतो धनम् ॥", "tr": "kṣaṇaśaḥ kaṇaśaś caiva vidyām arthaṃ ca sādhayet | kṣaṇa-tyāge kuto vidyā kaṇa-tyāge kuto dhanam ||", "en": "Acquire knowledge moment by moment and wealth grain by grain. Waste the moment and where is knowledge? Waste the grain and where is wealth?", "tk": "Small, consistent edges and daily learning compound into lasting growth.", "src": "Subhāṣita"}, {"sa": "अतिदानाद्बलिर्बद्धो ह्यतिमानात्सुयोधनः ।<br>विनष्टो रावणो लौल्यादति सर्वत्र वर्जयेत् ॥", "tr": "atidānād balir baddho hy atimānāt suyodhanaḥ | vinaṣṭo rāvaṇo laulyād ati sarvatra varjayet ||", "en": "Bali was bound by excessive generosity, Duryodhana fell through excessive pride, and Ravana was ruined by excessive greed. Avoid excess in everything.", "tk": "Over-leverage and over-trading end careers. Keep position sizes small and risk fixed.", "src": "Subhāṣita"}, {"sa": "अभ्यासवैराग्याभ्यां तन्निरोधः ॥", "tr": "abhyāsa-vairāgyābhyāṃ tan-nirodhaḥ ||", "en": "The fluctuations of the mind are stilled by practice and non-attachment.", "tk": "Practise on demo and in the market until your process is automatic, and stay detached from any single result.", "src": "Patañjali Yoga Sūtra 1.12"}];
